    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 202\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 6511, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the social services law, in relation to medical\n      assistance payments for clinical services provided to persons with\n      a traumatic brain injury\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would amend the Social Services  Law  to  increase  Medicaid\npayments  for clinical services without providing any funding to support\nit.\n \n  While I fully support the intent of this bill, the proposed reimburse-\nment increase should be addressed in the context  of  the  annual  State\nbudget  negotiations.  Without a budget appropriation, such spending and\nits intended impact cannot be realized. Further,  at  a  time  when  the\nFederal government has enacted, and is threatening additional, devastat-\ning cuts to the State's health care system, it would be irresponsible to\nincur  such  unbudgeted  costs.  In addition, this bill contains several\ntechnical flaws which would expand the scope of the  reimbursement,  and\nthe  corresponding  fiscal impact to the State, beyond what the legisla-\nture intended. For these reasons I am forced to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 202,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2017
